# Keep imported byte fixtures and their recorded SHA256 stable on Windows.
/development/m1/** -text
# The release key and the ssh-keygen probe vector are checked byte for byte (LF only; the probe signature covers the
# exact bytes): never convert their line endings on checkout (Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true).
/deploy/release/allowed_signers -text
/deploy/release/testdata/** -text
# The disk monitor is copied from a checkout to the Linux founder servers (bash scripts, systemd units, Python): keep LF
# on every checkout, Windows included.
/deploy/monitoring/** text eol=lf
# The extension's release package must be byte for byte the CI build on every checkout: the owner packages and signs it
# on Windows, where Git defaults to core.autocrlf=true, and a CRLF checkout once gave a package (f947c019...) whose 52
# text files differ from the CI build (6e38e72f...) only in their line endings. Keep LF in its text files on every
# checkout; text=auto leaves the PNG icons and screenshots binary. deploy/release/assemble_release.py also refuses
# an extension package with a CR in a text member.
/prototypes/pocol-extension/** text=auto eol=lf
